                        - <span class="citation">2015 SCC 1</span>
                    - <span class="report-citation">[2015] 1 SCR 3</span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">2015-01-16</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Supreme Court Judgments</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
                    <span>
                            Constitutional law<br/>
                    </span>
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    The onus rests on the party seeking to uphold the limitation of the Charter right, and the burden of proof is a preponderance of probabilities (<b>RJR-MacDonald</b> Inc. v. Canada (Attorney General), [1995] 3 S.C.R. 199, at paras. 137-38 (“<b>RJR-MacDonald</b> (1995)”). &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;For this reason, courts have not always insisted on direct proof of a relationship between the infringing measure and the legislative objective, accepting conclusions supported by logic and reason (<b>RJR-MacDonald</b> (1995), at para. 154; Ross v. New Brunswick School District No. 15, [1996] 1 S.C.R. 825, at para. 101). &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;(<b>RJR-MacDonald</b> (1995), at para. 160; see also Hutterian Brethren, at paras. 53-55; Health Services, at para. 150.) 
                </p>
                <div class="spacer">
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                </div>
        </div> 
        <div class="documents">
                <a target="_blank" href="/scc-csc/scc-csc/en/14577/1/document.do" title="Download the PDF version" class="matomo_download"><span class="decisia-icon icon-decisia-file-pdf"></span></a>
                <a href='javascript:void(0)' class='expand-result' title='Collapse result'></a>
        </div> 
    </div> 
    </div> 
</li>
    <li class="odd list-item-expanded">
<div class="number">
    <span class="digits">25.</span>
</div>
<div class="metadata">
    <div class="info" >
        <div class="subinfo">
            <h3>
                <span class="title"><a target="_parent" href="/scc-csc/scc-csc/en/item/17448/index.do?q=%22RJR-MacDonald%22">R. v. Beaudry</a></span>
                        - <span class="citation">2019 SCC 2</span>
                    - <span class="report-citation">[2019] 1 SCR 95</span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">2019-01-14</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Supreme Court Judgments</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    Referred to: Manitoba (Attorney General) v. Metropolitan Stores Ltd., [1987] 1 S.C.R. 110; <b>RJR — MacDonald</b> Inc. v. Canada (Attorney General), [1994] 1 S.C.R. 311. MOTION to stay the declaration of invalidity issued by the Court Martial Appeal Court of Canada (Bell C.J. and Gagné and Ouellette JJ.A.), 2018 CMAC 4, [2018] &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[2] The applicable criteria set out in Manitoba (Attorney General) v. Metropolitan Stores Ltd., [1987] 1 S.C.R. 110, and <b>RJR — MacDonald</b> Inc. v. Canada (Attorney General), [1994] 1 S.C.R. 311, are not in dispute. 
                </p>
                <div class="spacer">
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                        <span class="decisia-icon"></span>
                </div>
        </div> 
